$$
e^{-i\phi(z)}=a e^{-iz}
$$
for some $a>0$. Since $E$ is connected and both sides use the same branch,
$$
\boxed{\phi(z)=z+i\log a}.
$$
Thus $\phi$ is translation by a purely imaginary number.

